### Product Write Service + CDC pipeline - example requests (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### Start: docker compose (mysql-product, Kafka, kafka-connect, debezium-init, Elasticsearch)
###        -> eureka-server -> product-write-service -> product-service
### @write = source of truth (MySQL).  @read = projection (Elasticsearch).
### Between a write and the read check, wait about 1 second: the projection is
### ASYNCHRONOUS (eventual consistency). If a read still shows old data, run it again.

@write = http://localhost:8089/api/v1/products
@read = http://localhost:8081/api/v1/products
@connect = http://localhost:8083

### ===================== PIPELINE HEALTH =====================

### 1. Debezium connector status - expect connector AND task "state": "RUNNING"
GET {{connect}}/connectors/product-db-cdc/status

### 2. Write side health - expect "db" UP
GET http://localhost:8089/actuator/health

### 3. Read side: sample data arrived through CDC - expect "totalElements": 30
GET {{read}}?size=1

### ===================== CREATE =====================

### 4. Create in MySQL - expect 201, "version": 0, and a UUID id
POST {{write}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: cdc-demo-create-001

{
  "sku": "LAP-FRM-001",
  "name": "Framework Laptop 13",
  "description": "Modular, repairable 13.5-inch laptop with upgradeable memory and storage.",
  "brand": "Framework",
  "category": "laptop",
  "price": 1049.00,
  "ramGb": 16,
  "rating": 4.4,
  "tags": ["modular", "repairable", "windows"]
}

> {%
    client.global.set("productId", response.body.id);
%}

### 5. Source of truth - the row in MySQL
GET {{write}}/{{productId}}

### 6. Projection - SAME id, "version": 0, tags as an array (wait ~1 s after request 4)
GET {{read}}/{{productId}}

### 7. Searchable - expect the Framework laptop in the results
GET {{read}}?q=repairable

### ===================== UPDATE (optimistic locking) =====================

### 8. Update with the CURRENT version 0 - expect 200 and "version": 1
PUT {{write}}/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 0,
  "name": "Framework Laptop 13 (2026 Edition)",
  "description": "Modular, repairable 13.5-inch laptop with upgradeable memory and storage.",
  "brand": "Framework",
  "category": "laptop",
  "price": 999.00,
  "ramGb": 32,
  "rating": 4.5,
  "tags": ["modular", "repairable", "windows"]
}

### 9. Projection updated - expect price 999.00, ramGb 32, "version": 1
GET {{read}}/{{productId}}

### 10. Update with an OLD version (0) - expect 409 "Stale version"; MySQL and ES unchanged
PUT {{write}}/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 0,
  "name": "Lost update attempt",
  "brand": "Framework",
  "category": "laptop",
  "price": 1.00
}

### ===================== VALIDATION & CONFLICTS =====================

### 11. Duplicate SKU (case-insensitive) - expect 409 "Duplicate SKU"
POST {{write}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "lap-frm-001",
  "name": "Duplicate",
  "brand": "Framework",
  "category": "laptop",
  "price": 10.00
}

### 12. Invalid body - expect 400 with errors for sku, name, price, rating and tags
POST {{write}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "bad sku!",
  "name": "",
  "brand": "Test",
  "category": "laptop",
  "price": -5,
  "rating": 7,
  "tags": ["Has Spaces"]
}

### 13. Update without version - expect 400 "version is required"
PUT {{write}}/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "No version",
  "brand": "Framework",
  "category": "laptop",
  "price": 10.00
}

### ===================== DELETE =====================

### 14. Delete in MySQL - expect 204
DELETE {{write}}/{{productId}}

### 15. Projection removed - expect 404 from the READ side (wait ~1 s)
GET {{read}}/{{productId}}

### 16. Delete again - expect 404 from the write side
DELETE {{write}}/{{productId}}
